A||||8||afRaceR||headlight motor||||1||
Z||000000||afRaceR||11-28-2000||12:03 AM||||Hi.......new to the forum but not to Fieros.<BR>I've had my fiero for a while but just recently found this sight.<P>I just got a problem with the passenger headlight motor. It goes up fine, but when it goes down, the motor doesn't stop and there's kind of a grinding noise. Anybody know what this is? and is it an easy fix?<P>thanks in advance||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ed||11-28-2000||12:16 AM|||| <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/headlights.html</A> <P>And check the archives.||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||11-28-2000||07:59 AM||||its the plastic gear inside that has been stripped.  There was talk of just opening up the motor and flipping around the gear, did that didnt help, so i bought another motor from junkyard.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||11-28-2000||10:38 AM||||Go to rodney dickmans site and buy the gear set for $45, that's exacty what my headlight did to me and I got the set and replaced them, they work great now.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||11-28-2000||10:51 AM||||What year is your Fiero?<P>If you have an 87 or 88, you can probably just get the bushing set drom Rodney for about $7 or $8.  His directions are easy to follow.  The bushings turn to dust over time causing the problem you describe and more.<P>If you have an 84-86 model, you will probably need the full repair set discussed above.  The earlier motors are more complex and often require more parts to fix properly.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||afRaceR||11-28-2000||10:06 PM||||$50?!?!? I think I'll just get a good used motor and go through it real well. $50 just seems like too much for a little gear. Thanks everyone for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||11-28-2000||10:15 PM||||Just keep in mind that the $50 (if you have a 84-86) should bring the motor to like new condition.  It should then last another 12-15 years.  You don't know how long a used motor will last.  They might be subject to the same problems you are now experiencing.<P>Rodney's price is reasonable compared to the cost of a new motor IMO.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||PlasticWrapd||11-29-2000||05:22 AM||||Just a note...  if you opt for the used headlight motor, the driver's side motor from a 82-86 Firebird is the same part as the passenger side motor on a 84-86 Fiero.  Ask for the Firebird part and you'll save some $$$.  I paid $35 for the Firebird part and the salvage yard wanted $50 for the Fiero part!  Go figure||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rodney||11-29-2000||09:47 PM||||A new OEM gear and the 2 internal bumpers, a packet of some expensive silicone grease, and screws to bolt the motor back together is $21.50 per motor. I include rebuilding instructions and a 2 page trouble shooting write up. Add the brush/contact assembly for $21 more. Last list price on the brush/contact assembly alone from GM in '92 when it was discontinued was around $39. I do not see my prices as being too high. ||||reg||1
